Do not compose names on their way to the NFS server.

The client mounted with `nfc`, which converts every name it sends into
Normalization Form C. What comes back from readdir is the name as the volume
stores it. A name stored decomposed is therefore listed but never resolved:
lookup, open, rename and unlink all compose it first and match nothing.

Measured on a 247 GB NTFS volume: 4 of 28 entries were stored decomposed, and
every one of them answered ENOENT on stat while appearing in the listing. The
folders holding them could not be emptied, so Finder refused to delete them and
said the item was in use.

Names now go to the server as they came from it, whatever form that is.

